jffs2: do not reserve the deflate workspace when nothing can compress

jffs2_compressors_init() allocates the zlib deflate workspace at filesystem
init, before any mount. With MAX_WBITS and MAX_MEM_LEVEL that is 64 KiB of
window, 64 KiB of prev, 64 KiB of head and 64 KiB of overlay plus the state
structure: about 264 KiB, taken with vmalloc and held for the life of the
system.

This board builds with CONFIG_JFFS2_CMODE_NONE, so jffs2_compress() takes the
JFFS2_COMPR_MODE_NONE arm of its switch and returns immediately; the deflate
path is never entered and that quarter of a megabyte is never touched.

It costs more than its size. NOMMU has no vmalloc area -- mm/nommu.c makes
vmalloc() a kmalloc() -- so a 262 KiB request goes to the page allocator as
get_order(262144 + sizeof(deflate_workspace)), which is order 7: a contiguous
512 KiB block, held forever. Contiguous blocks are exactly what a fork on this
machine needs and cannot get; /proc/buddyinfo on an idle board shows a single
free order-7 block, and a fork of bash has been seen to fail with 112 KiB
available.

The inflate workspace stays unconditionally: the shipped /etc and /home images
are built by mkfs.jffs2 with compression on, so reading them needs it whatever
the write-side mode is.

CMODE_NONE is only a default: `mount -o compr=zlib` (or a remount) overrides
it per superblock and would reach jffs2_zlib_compress() with a NULL
workspace, and zlib_deflateInit2() stores through that pointer before it
validates anything. So under CMODE_NONE the zlib compressor also refuses to
compress: jffs2_compress() falls back to storing the data uncompressed, which
is what the mode meant in the first place. Decompression is unaffected.

--- a/fs/jffs2/compr_zlib.c
+++ b/fs/jffs2/compr_zlib.c
@@ -42,6 +42,12 @@
 
 static int __init alloc_workspaces(void)
 {
+	/* With CMODE_NONE jffs2_compress() returns before it ever reaches a
+	 * compressor, so the deflate workspace -- about 264 KiB of vmalloc,
+	 * held for the life of the system -- is never touched. Reading still
+	 * needs inflate: the factory /etc and /home images are compressed.
+	 */
+#ifndef CONFIG_JFFS2_CMODE_NONE
 	def_strm.workspace = vmalloc(zlib_deflate_workspacesize(MAX_WBITS,
 							MAX_MEM_LEVEL));
 	if (!def_strm.workspace)
@@ -49,9 +55,12 @@
 
 	jffs2_dbg(1, "Allocated %d bytes for deflate workspace\n",
 		  zlib_deflate_workspacesize(MAX_WBITS, MAX_MEM_LEVEL));
+#endif
 	inf_strm.workspace = vmalloc(zlib_inflate_workspacesize());
 	if (!inf_strm.workspace) {
+#ifndef CONFIG_JFFS2_CMODE_NONE
 		vfree(def_strm.workspace);
+#endif
 		return -ENOMEM;
 	}
 	jffs2_dbg(1, "Allocated %d bytes for inflate workspace\n",
@@ -61,7 +70,9 @@
 
 static void free_workspaces(void)
 {
+#ifndef CONFIG_JFFS2_CMODE_NONE
 	vfree(def_strm.workspace);
+#endif
 	vfree(inf_strm.workspace);
 }
 #else
@@ -78,6 +89,13 @@
 	if (*dstlen <= STREAM_END_SPACE)
 		return -1;
 
+#ifdef CONFIG_JFFS2_CMODE_NONE
+	/* No deflate workspace was allocated (see alloc_workspaces), so this
+	 * must never run: compr=zlib on the mount line is the one way in.
+	 * Returning -1 makes jffs2_compress() store the node uncompressed.
+	 */
+	return -1;
+#endif
 	mutex_lock(&deflate_mutex);
 
 	if (Z_OK != zlib_deflateInit(&def_strm, 3)) {
